    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3204" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ap-prŏbus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adp-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		ad <i>intens.;</i> cf.
		apprimus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very good</i> or <i>excellent;</i> as an
				adj. once: adulescens adprobus, Caecil. ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 7, 7,
				9</span></i>.—Once as adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ap-prŏbē</span></b> : 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ni me ille et ego illum novissem adprobe,</span>”
				<i>very well</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Trin. 4, 2, 117</span></i>
			.</div>
